Statime (github.com/teodly/statime, branch inferno-dev, 244f20a5): publish
the PTP port state to a file.

Why: the USB-AoIP control page has to tell its user whether the unit's
clock has a leader, the first thing a new unit on a network gets wrong.
Statime logs port-state changes at info; the unit runs it at warn, where it
says nothing on gaining a leader, and the journal rate limit can drop the
one line it prints on losing one.

What: when the environment variable STATIME_PORT_STATE_FILE is set,
set_forced_port_state() writes one line to that file, by a temporary file
and a rename, each time a port's state changes:

    state=Slave port=1 leader=<clock identity and port, hex>
    state=Master port=1 leader=
    state=Listening port=1 leader=

Slave means the port is following a leader. Without the variable the code
does nothing, so a build with this patch and no variable behaves as the
pinned one. The write happens in the thread that runs the port, on a state
change only; on a tmpfs it does not wait for a disk.

Status: DRAFT, 2026-11-10. Written from a read of the source and
compile-checked in CI on arm64; never run. It changes the Statime binary,
which is part of the audio path's build: the installer applies it only with
PTP_STATE=1, and a unit built with it is a new operating point until
measured (docs/INSTALL.md, "Showing whether the clock has a leader").

License: as Statime (Apache-2.0 OR MIT).

diff --git a/statime/src/port/mod.rs b/statime/src/port/mod.rs
index d9a5461..24083a1 100644
--- a/statime/src/port/mod.rs
+++ b/statime/src/port/mod.rs
@@ -662,6 +662,30 @@ impl<L, A, R, C: Clock, F: Filter, S> Port<'_, L, A, R, C, F, S> {
             state
         );
         core::mem::swap(&mut self.port_state, &mut state);
+        // Publish the port state, for whatever needs to know whether this
+        // follower has a leader: at loglevel warn nothing else says so. One
+        // line, replaced atomically at each change (changes are rare: a
+        // leader appearing, going away or being replaced). Off unless
+        // STATIME_PORT_STATE_FILE names a file; a failed write is ignored,
+        // the clock does not depend on it.
+        if let Ok(path) = std::env::var("STATIME_PORT_STATE_FILE") {
+            let leader = match &self.port_state {
+                PortState::Slave(slave) => {
+                    let master = slave.remote_master();
+                    hex::encode(master.clock_identity.0)
+                        + &hex::encode(master.port_number.to_be_bytes())
+                }
+                _ => std::string::String::new(),
+            };
+            let line = std::format!(
+                "state={} port={} leader={}\n",
+                self.port_state, self.port_identity.port_number, leader
+            );
+            let temporary = std::format!("{path}.tmp");
+            if std::fs::write(&temporary, line).is_ok() {
+                let _ = std::fs::rename(&temporary, &path);
+            }
+        }
         if matches!(state, PortState::Slave(_) | PortState::Faulty)
             || matches!(self.port_state, PortState::Faulty)
         {
